nature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Verify attestation — `[non-codebase]` AC\n\n**The verify suite is green for this change. CI exit status: SUCCESS (0).**\n\n- Change: Gerrit 2992, patch set 1, revision `aaaf20bba76a36fa52a733b2939f013e2c58d94c`\n- CI run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/35488608320\n- Verdict: `rebar-ci-bot` cast **`Verified +1` — SUCCESS**, every job green (lint +\n  type-check, the `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` gating pytest cell and the rest of the matrix,\n  sandbox enforcement, mutation, artifact-probe, authorship, optionality,\n  scanner-integration).\n- Landed: submitted revision-scoped and merged to `main`.\n\n`AGENTS.md` defines `make test` as selecting exactly what CI's gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13`\ncell selects, and describes a local `make verify` as \"the locally checkable **half** of\n`Verified`\". CI ran that selection plus the rest of the matrix and passed, so this is the\nstronger of the two signals.","timestamp":1789882780903345493},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion gate returned FAIL at 2026-09-19T23:2x — investigated before re-running, and the FAIL was not about this ticket's criteria.\n\nThe gate was started without an explicit `ref`, so it verified against the store repository's checked-out HEAD (`e900fa14ad5`, 2026-09-19 00:40 UTC) rather than current `origin/main`. This ticket's fix merged as `e8bdeb9a813`, which is reachable from `origin/main` but **not** from that stale HEAD, so the \"work landed\" precheck failed before any criteria were judged.\n\nConfirming evidence: zero `COMPLETION_VERDICT` events were written to this ticket's directory. A real criteria judgement always writes one with a per-criterion `met` array. The control is `16c9-a42d` and `5a31-8c91`, verified in the same session with an explicit `ref` — both PASSed and both recorded a verdict.\n\nRe-running now with `ref=d5c325a4170dfee29af010164a1cc2e3289cdc83`. The description and acceptance criteria were not changed, because nothing about them was implicated.\n\nThe misleading failure shape is filed separately as `selective-dermic-coelacanth` (c6fb-49cf), linked `discovered_from` this ticket.","timestamp":1789886952116737013},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"**Correction — my previous comment on this ticket was wrong.** The stale-store-HEAD diagnosis does not hold, and the FAIL is genuine.\n\nI tested it and it was refuted three ways: `--ref` defaults to `origin/main` (not the store HEAD) per `rebar verify-completion --help`; re-running with an explicit `ref=d5c325a4170` still FAILed; and `16c9-a42d` / `5a31-8c91`, which PASSed, are equally unreachable from that stale HEAD and equally record `file_impact`. Disregard the earlier comment.\n\n**The actual root cause: change 2992 was incomplete.** It updated `CONTRIBUTING.md` but never touched `docs/releasing.md`, which is in this ticket's own recorded `file_impact`.\n\nVerifier findings at `ref=d5c325a4170dfee29af010164a1cc2e3289cdc83` (2 unmet criteria, both `severity: high`):\n\n1. `docs/releasing.md:590-596` is missing the `mcp` major-version ignore statement entirely — searching the file for `major-ignore` returns no matches — and still carries the stale \"This is the pip/pydantic GitHub-native shape\" wording the approach section said to replace.\n2. Consequently the bug itself is only partially resolved: the defect still reproduces in `docs/releasing.md`.\n\n5 of 7 criteria were met, including the `[non-codebase]` verify-suite criterion.\n\n**Remediation in flight.** Worktree `fix-f3b2-releasing-docs` at `origin/main`. `docs/releasing.md` now names both ecosystems with their groups, the committed `uv.lock` and its consumers, the `mcp` major-ignore with patch and security updates staying enabled, and drops the stale pip/pydantic sentence while keeping the \"not the bespoke Gerrit-pushing bot\" contrast. Grounded against `.github/dependabot.yml:1-12,27-37` rather than copied from `CONTRIBUTING.md`. `make verify` running; Gerrit change to follow.\n\nThe async surface's failure to expose these findings — which cost a duplicate billable verifier run to recover — is filed as `selective-dermic-coelacanth` (c6fb-49cf), linked `discovered_from` this ticket.","timestamp":1789887483750426792},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"**Addendum — which tree the verifier actually read.**\n\nMy previous comment said the findings came from `ref=d5c325a4170`. They did not. The MCP workspace at `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code` was checked out at `8f7417079a` (2026-09-19 02:18 UTC), 28.5 hours behind `main`, and every completion run read that tree regardless of the `ref` passed. Change 2992's merge commit `e8bdeb9a813` is **not** an ancestor of `8f7417079a`, so the verifier could not see this ticket's fix at all. Filed on `working-carnelian-bobwhite` (8806-198c) with the measurements.\n\n**The conclusion is unchanged, and I re-confirmed it directly rather than relying on the verifier.** Against the current tip of `main`:\n\n```\ngit show origin/main:docs/releasing.md | grep -n -i 'major'\n552:   a major bump, with a deprecation window).\n```\n\nThe only `major` match is an unrelated sentence about deprecation windows. The `mcp` major-version ignore statement is absent from `docs/releasing.md` at `origin/main`, so the fix genuinely is incomplete and the remediation in flight is still required.\n\nNet: the FAIL verdict was right, its stated reasoning was about the wrong tree, and the underlying gap is real. I will re-verify with `ref=origin/main` once the follow-up change merges.","timestamp":1789888174632872831}],"created_at":1788602159470505001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"72f5c3bd-8401-4cfe-b993-9ac0f8cc2055","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4312-882e-e92c-4da5"},{"link_uuid":"5af6159b-4864-497c-bab1-8b4d3df1c3f5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5ace-8f33-a8a4-4112"},{"link_uuid":"6d4fe73a-e7d3-4680-a9e2-608fe50d7398","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"95d5-2344-6646-40cc"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`CONTRIBUTING.md:689-697` says dependency updates use security alerts only, not version-bump PRs; says `.github/dependabot.yml` configures GitHub-Actions monthly version-update PRs; and says there is intentionally no `pip` ecosystem entry because core dependencies are unpinned. `docs/releasing.md:590-595` repeats the stale one-ecosystem guidance by saying `.github/dependabot.yml` runs GitHub-Actions version updates monthly and calls that the pip/pydantic GitHub-native shape.\n\nThe current source of truth is `.github/dependabot.yml`. Its header at `.github/dependabot.yml:1-8` says Dependabot opens advisory PRs for monthly GitHub Actions and weekly uv updates, maintainers reproduce accepted bumps through Gerrit, the uv entry updates the committed `uv.lock`, and security alerts remain enabled independently of version-update PRs. The active entries configure `github-actions` on a monthly cadence with group `github-actions` at `.github/dependabot.yml:15-24`, and `uv` on a weekly cadence with group `uv-lock` at `.github/dependabot.yml:27-39`. Major `mcp` version updates are ignored at `.github/dependabot.yml:35-37` while patch and security updates remain enabled per `.github/dependabot.yml:10-12`.\n\n## Approach\nUpdate `CONTRIBUTING.md` and `docs/releasing.md` to use `.github/dependabot.yml` as the source of truth. The prose should state the two ecosystems, the two cadences, the lock-backed uv behavior, the advisory PR workflow through Gerrit, and the `mcp` major-version ignore rule without copying every Dependabot key.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `CONTRIBUTING.md` removes the claim at lines 689-690 that dependency updates use security alerts only and replaces it with a statement that Dependabot opens advisory version-update PRs for monthly GitHub Actions and weekly uv updates while security alerts remain enabled independently.\n- [x] `CONTRIBUTING.md` replaces the Actions-only claim at line 691 with the current `.github/dependabot.yml:15-39` configuration: `github-actions` runs monthly in group `github-actions`, and `uv` runs weekly in group `uv-lock`.\n- [x] `CONTRIBUTING.md` replaces the no-`pip` rationale at lines 695-697 with the current lock-backed uv rationale from `.github/dependabot.yml:5-8`: uv updates the committed `uv.lock`, published metadata keeps unpinned minimums, and a pip entry would change nothing.\n- [x] `CONTRIBUTING.md` documents the `mcp` major-version ignore from `.github/dependabot.yml:35-37` while stating that patch updates and security updates remain enabled.\n- [x] `docs/releasing.md` replaces the one-ecosystem guidance at lines 590-595 with the same monthly GitHub Actions, weekly uv, committed-`uv.lock`, Gerrit-advisory workflow, and `mcp` major-ignore statements used in `CONTRIBUTING.md`.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The full verify suite is green for this change, with the run and its\n      exit code recorded on this ticket. The authoritative signal is the Gerrit `Verified`\n      vote on this change's patch set, which runs the same selection `make test` runs.\n      provenance: environment=github-actions-hosted-runner; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — CI run 35488608320 executed the gating suite against Gerrit change 2992 patch set 1 (revision aaaf20bba76a36fa52a733b2939f013e2c58d94c) and concluded SUCCESS, casting `Verified +1`; that run is the same merge gate that admits the change to `main`, so its exit status is the authoritative verify result rather than a simulation of one.\n\n## Testing\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` from the repository checkout and land only if it exits 0.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","reason":"Align contributor dependency-update guidance with monthly GitHub Actions, weekly uv lockfile updates, and the mcp major-version ignore rule."},{"path":"docs/releasing.md","reason":"Align release dependency-update guidance with the active Dependabot ecosystems, cadences, and advisory Gerrit workflow."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","5ace-8f33-a8a4-4112"],["relates_to","95d5-2344-6646-40cc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"89cdb487-9334-4381-9d6a-dd3e549f79a0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["documentation","dependabot","drift"],"ticket_id":"f3b2-6bb8-a643-4025","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Align Dependabot documentation with weekly uv and monthly Actions updates","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4b53ec6c-18ab-4311-9bf4-d2938ba3c5bf","94eb83c1-514d-4fa3-b5ad-3fed64b30b90","5b42bd70-4f09-4ff0-ac96-0cc886330172","27ee9ec9-35ae-4d8f-a731-d0aba5072c14","89cdb487-9334-4381-9d6a-dd3e549f79a0","993acfcd-9f0e-4003-bd81-eab4de6548a2","5af6159b-4864-497c-bab1-8b4d3df1c3f5","c6a487b6-335f-4a4e-9649-273176637fbb","ade26fa0-c7df-4a72-84ba-4b9c08cde92e","10b38ac7-5ab6-4ddd-b6a4-24ecb3baefc8","42aa481a-723e-43cf-9c81-a7c73b254270","f250dd8e-35d2-400d-9f4d-c99f275b8dc4","6d4fe73a-e7d3-4680-a9e2-608fe50d7398"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-